i.github.com/users/mbucchia","html_url":"https://github.com/mbucchia","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-16T17:15:13Z","updated_at":"2025-03-16T17:15:13Z","body":"> 4.x very recently changed to `#pragma once` instead of header guards (#102298), the documentation may be out of date.\r\n\r\nUnderstood. I will change my new files to use the pragmas. Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2727548494/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2728045411","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104207#issuecomment-2728045411","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104207","id":2728045411,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6imqtj","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-17T03:43:16Z","updated_at":"2025-03-17T03:43:16Z","body":"Just giving this a first look and all seems pretty good. I don't know the DX12 backend well enough to give any insight on that so will need @clayjohn or @DarioSamo to verify the changes.\r\n\r\nI'll find some time to do some testing on my end this week.\r\n\r\nRe your comment here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/86283#issuecomment-2727254988\r\nWith WMR itself defuncts, do we want to put hacks like this in or just make note of them for anyone that wants to custom build for WMR?\r\nI'm assuming here that SteamVR and other PC OpenXR runtimes will work with DX12 as well, the main goal here would be for those who wish to use the DX12 renderer on windows to be able to do VR with Godot.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2728045411/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2728056806","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104207#issuecomment-2728056806","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104207","id":2728056806,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6imtfm","user":{"login":"mbucchia","id":69611560,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NjExNTYw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69611560?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia","html_url":"https://github.com/mbucchia","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-17T03:50:59Z","updated_at":"2025-03-17T05:55:23Z","body":"Thank you Bastiaan! Please suggest some more testing as well if you want. I saw a couple of XR demo samples, maybe I will give those a shot. If you have a stress test let me know.\r\n\r\n> Re your comment here: [#86283 (comment)](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/86283#issuecomment-2727254988)\r\n> With WMR itself defuncts, do we want to put hacks like this in or just make note of them for anyone that wants to custom build for WMR?\r\n\r\nI'm a little bit torn yeah. I think you really want to get rid of this warning message that calls specifically incompatibility with WMR today. D3D support was an avenue for that. \r\n\r\nBut also as I mentioned, I don't know if the issue will remain specific to WMR _if_ a platform begins to use D3D12 as its **internal** gfx API in the future. There is none today AFAICT (most use D3D11 for composition inside the runtime). I might talk some more to the D3D team at Microsoft about these scenarios of \"mixed usage\" of Agility SDK. Definitely nothing actionable on the current PR though.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2728056806/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2808138829","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104207#issuecomment-2808138829","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104207","id":2808138829,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nYMxN","user":{"login":"mbucchia","id":69611560,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NjExNTYw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69611560?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia","html_url":"https://github.com/mbucchia","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-16T03:33:19Z","updated_at":"2025-04-16T03:33:19Z","body":"> Sorry it took me awhile to get to this and properly test it.\r\n> \r\n> Functionally this is working great for me. I've tested it both with the demo project on my original issue and running OpenXR with DX12 over SteamVR.\r\n\r\nNo worries, and thanks for the testing!\r\n\r\n> My only question is whether you added the `d3d12_hooks` logic because Vulkan had it, or if it actually is used? None of the methods are implemented so I think you can leave this out.\r\n> In Vulkan this is required because we let OpenXR handle the Vulkan instance creation, but I don't think that is required for DX.\r\n\r\nIt's actually used and I did copy the general idea from Vulkan. But maybe there is a better way of doing it.\r\n\r\nThe methods are implemented in `openxr_d3d12_extension.cpp` since the class `OpenXRD3D12Extension` inherits from `D3D12Hooks`. I am using it to pass around the D3D12 command queue from the renderer initialization for example. See `rendering_device_driver_d3d12.cpp` L2351 for example. Is there a better way to store/capture the outcome of the renderer initialization otherwise?\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2808138829/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2808557905","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104207#issuecomment-2808557905","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104207","id":2808557905,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nZzFR","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-16T06:46:35Z","updated_at":"2025-04-16T06:46:35Z","body":"> The methods are implemented in `openxr_d3d12_extension.cpp` since the class `OpenXRD3D12Extension` inherits from `D3D12Hooks`. I am using it to pass around the D3D12 command queue from the renderer initialization for example. See `rendering_device_driver_d3d12.cpp` L2351 for example. Is there a better way to store/capture the outcome of the renderer initialization otherwise?\r\n\r\nAh, that makes sense, totally missed that. Cool!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2808557905/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2814251068","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104207#issuecomment-2814251068","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104207","id":2814251068,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nvhA8","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-18T00:26:21Z","updated_at":"2025-04-18T00:26:21Z","body":"XR Meeting, we're happy for this to be merged as is, we can do any minor cleanup later.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2814251068/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2814252263","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104207#issuecomment-2814252263","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104207","id":2814252263,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nvhTn","user":{"login":"mbucchia","id":69611560,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NjExNTYw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69611560?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia","html_url":"https://github.com/mbucchia","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-18T00:27:48Z","updated_at":"2025-04-18T00:27:48Z","body":"I meant to test on AMD and Intel GPU as well, give me maybe a day or two.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2814252263/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816578580","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104207#issuecomment-2816578580","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104207","id":2816578580,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6n4ZQU","user":{"login":"mbucchia","id":69611560,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NjExNTYw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69611560?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia","html_url":"https://github.com/mbucchia","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-19T07:00:52Z","updated_at":"2025-04-19T07:00:52Z","body":"I was able to test with an AMD RDNA2 card successfully. I am not able to make my Intel ARC card work today (nothing to do with the change or Godot, the card isn't enumerating in Windows). I will circle back later, not worth blocking merge IMO.\r\n\r\nI rebased against latest upstream, rebuilt and ran a quick sanity test. Added stub method `get_density_map()` (like it is done in the OpenGL backend as well - though I will probably get back to proper support for that, since it looks interesting). Fixed the couple of blank spaces suggestions in the process.\r\n\r\nI pushed my rebase in two times, 1st push is rebase only (no changes to the code, as there were no conflicts) and 2nd push is the small delta I've described above.\r\n\r\n@BastiaanOlij, please go ahead and merge when ready. I recommend editing the final commit message to remove the bullet points of testing (see marker in my PR description, with the little scissors 8< 8<)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816578580/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816907660","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104207#issuecomment-2816907660","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104207","id":2816907660,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6n5pmM","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cl